From ba26b02b0e258dc4c11067b8c655f5abb91dfb9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "MOTOR-46 (Claude)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:39:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tabs: shared pinned tab Mac test confirms the pinned close
 toast

Since Chromium 156, chrome::CloseTab() on a pinned tab first shows the
kClosePinnedTab toast and closes only on the second command, so
CloseTabShortCutShouldBeDisabled saw 2 tabs after one IDC_CLOSE_TAB
(LOCAL-19, 3.1.2). Issue the command twice; the Cmd+W part of the test
is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MwmK2juPkbC58kEi4QFeyU
---
 .../tabs/test/shared_pinned_tab_service_browsertest_mac.mm  | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/browser/ui/tabs/test/shared_pinned_tab_service_browsertest_mac.mm b/browser/ui/tabs/test/shared_pinned_tab_service_browsertest_mac.mm
index c1046d3c..8ea7d50c 100644
--- a/browser/ui/tabs/test/shared_pinned_tab_service_browsertest_mac.mm
+++ b/browser/ui/tabs/test/shared_pinned_tab_service_browsertest_mac.mm
@@ -52,7 +52,11 @@ IN_PROC_BROWSER_TEST_F(SharedPinnedTabServiceBrowserTest,
   // Then the tab should not be closed.
   EXPECT_EQ(browser->tab_strip_model()->count(), 2);
 
-  // When other ways to close the tab are tried
+  // When other ways to close the tab are tried. Since Chromium 156, closing a
+  // pinned tab with IDC_CLOSE_TAB first shows a confirmation toast
+  // (ToastId::kClosePinnedTab) and only the second command closes it.
+  chrome::ExecuteCommand(browser, IDC_CLOSE_TAB);
+  EXPECT_EQ(browser->tab_strip_model()->count(), 2);
   chrome::ExecuteCommand(browser, IDC_CLOSE_TAB);
 
   // Then tab should be closed
